---
import BaseCrisp from "../layouts/BaseCrisp.astro";

// one green check, reused across pricing lists
const check = `<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="#1f9d64" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>`;
const play = `<svg width="20" height="24" viewBox="0 0 26 30" fill="#fff" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 0 L26 15 L0 30 Z"/></svg>`;
---

<BaseCrisp>
  {/* ===== Hero ===== */}
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <span class="pill"><span class="t">OPEN SOURCE</span> self-host · your keys · 0% markup</span>
    <h1>The flight recorder<br><span class="thin">for AI agents.</span></h1>
    <p class="hsub">Autonomous agents fail without crashing — a clean 200, well-formed tokens, and the run already three steps off course. Tracelane records every run to a tamper-evident ledger you can prove.</p>
    <div class="hcta"><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-lava">Be first to know →</a><a href="https://github.com/tracelane" rel="me noopener" class="btn btn-ghost">GitHub</a></div>
    <div class="hmicro">apache-2.0 core · self-host anywhere · no credit card</div>

    {/* Hero video stage — drop /hero.mp4 + /hero-poster.jpg; overlay shows until then */}
    <div class="stage-wrap reveal">
      <div class="win-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="addr">tracelane — replay</span></div>
      <div class="stage" id="hero-stage">
        <video id="hero-video" class="stage-video" poster="/hero-poster.jpg" preload="none" playsinline controls style="display:none">
          <source src="/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
        <button class="stage-overlay" id="hero-play" type="button" aria-label="Play the tracelane story">
          <span class="play" set:html={play} />
          <span class="cap">Watch a run recorded, replayed, and verified</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Keyword pillars — the spine (re-skinned Record / Replay / Prove) ===== */}
  <section id="pillars" style="padding:0 0 44px"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="pillars reveal">
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Gateway</div><p>One endpoint in front of every model. Your keys, 0% markup, bounded overhead — every call captured in full fidelity.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Observability</div><p>Step-level traces — every prompt, tool call, latency and cost, down to the exact call that broke.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Audit</div><p>A tamper-evident, Ed25519-signed ledger. Verify the whole chain yourself, offline.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Provider marquee ===== */}
  <div class="marquee"><div class="wrap mrow">
    <span>OpenAI</span><span>Anthropic</span><span>Google</span><span>Mistral</span><span>Bedrock</span><span>Groq</span><b>30+ providers</b>
  </div></div>

  {/* ===== Problem trio ===== */}
  <section><div class="wrap center">
    <div class="eyebrow">Why agent failures stay invisible</div>
    <div class="stitle">A clean 200 tells you nothing.</div>
    <div class="trio reveal">
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">01</div><h4>State drift compounds</h4><p>A bad tool output at step 2 corrupts every step after it. The model keeps going, confidently, further from the goal.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">02</div><h4>Success codes lie</h4><p>A 200 and clean tokens say nothing about whether the state is still valid three steps later. Tracelane reconstructs the causal path, not the request log.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">03</div><h4>Tools run code</h4><p>Every tool call executes on your behalf. The ledger is the cryptographic record of exactly what ran.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Signature verify block ===== */}
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="verify reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Independently verifiable</div>
      <h2>You don't trust us. You verify us.</h2>
      <p class="vs">SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed every 100 events. Anchored batches carry a resolved Sigstore Rekor v2 inclusion proof (best-effort; universal per-run anchoring on the roadmap). Tampering means breaking the math — not editing a row.</p>
      <div class="vterm">
        <div><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tlane verify &lt;trace-id&gt;</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">signature valid</span> <span class="p">(Ed25519, Merkle root)</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">hash chain unbroken</span> <span class="p">(SHA-256)</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">tamper-evident: yes</span><span class="cursor"></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Migration ===== */}
  <section id="migrate"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Migration</div>
    <div class="stitle">Coming from a tool that got acquired or breached?</div>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0;text-align:left">Importers land with V1 — no data leaves your infrastructure during migration.</p>
    <div class="grid2 reveal">
      <div class="tcard"><h4>From Helicone</h4><p style="margin-top:8px">For teams on Helicone after it entered maintenance mode (Mintlify acquisition, Mar 2026). One-command import of traces, configs, prompts, and rate-limit rules — lands with V1.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><h4>From LiteLLM</h4><p style="margin-top:8px">After CVE-2026-33634 (Mar 24) and CVE-2026-42208 (Apr 24). Drop-in gateway replacement; config import lands with V1. Sigstore-signed releases, SLSA Build L3 provenance, Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived tokens.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Audit ledger ===== */}
  <section id="audit" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">The audit ledger</div>
    <div class="stitle">Every run. On the record. Provably.</div>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0;text-align:left;max-width:640px">Each event is hash-chained with SHA-256. Every 100 events the Merkle root is signed with Ed25519. Verify the whole chain offline — tampering means breaking SHA-256 or forging a signature, not editing a row.</p>
    <div class="grid3-cards reveal">
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">eu ai act</div><p>Article 12 export pack — full audit trail for high-risk AI systems. Annex III enforcement provisionally deferred to Dec 2, 2027 (Digital Omnibus political agreement, May 7, 2026; pending formal adoption — <a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" rel="noopener">details</a>); the ledger ships at V1.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">india dpdp</div><p>Phase II enforcement Nov 13, 2026. EU data residency at V1; India residency on the roadmap, on demand. Audit-log retention configurable.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">hipaa</div><p>BAA available on Business tier. PII redaction inline. Provider keys envelope-encrypted.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Dev / code ===== */}
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap dev">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">For developers</div>
      <h2>One line.<br>Every provider.</h2>
      <p>Point any OpenAI-compatible client at Tracelane. Your code doesn't change.</p>
      <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-lava">Read the docs →</a>
      <div class="dstats">
        <div class="dstat"><div class="n">30+</div><div class="l">providers</div></div>
        <div class="dstat"><div class="n">0%</div><div class="l">markup</div></div>
        <div class="dstat"><div class="n">&lt;15ms</div><div class="l">overhead*</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="codepanel">
      <div class="ptabs"><div class="ptab on">Python</div><div class="ptab">TypeScript</div><div class="ptab">cURL</div></div>
      <div class="code"><span class="c"># any OpenAI client, one URL change</span>
<span class="k">from</span> openai <span class="k">import</span> OpenAI

client = <span class="f">OpenAI</span>(
    base_url=<span class="s">"https://gateway.tracelane.dev/v1"</span>,
    api_key=<span class="s">"tlane_..."</span>,
)

resp = client.chat.completions.<span class="f">create</span>(
    model=<span class="s">"claude-sonnet-4-6"</span>,
    messages=[&#123;<span class="s">"role"</span>:<span class="s">"user"</span>,<span class="s">"content"</span>:<span class="s">"ship it"</span>&#125;],
)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap footnote">*p95 overhead target, excluding provider time — measured numbers publish as the Tracelane Reliability Benchmark v1.0 at launch.</div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Roadmap — aspirational, no dates ===== */}
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap road">
    <div class="eyebrow">What we're building next</div>
    <div class="stitle">Imagine what you'll see.</div>
    <p class="lead">V1 is the recorder. Next, it starts to reason with you.</p>
    <div class="roadgrid reveal">
      <div class="rc"><div class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4 6h16M4 12h10M4 18h13" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><h4>Ask your traces</h4><p>Query a thousand runs in plain English — and get real trace IDs back.</p></div>
      <div class="rc"><div class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 3v10M8 8v5M16 6v7M5 11v2M19 10v3" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><h4>Voice, on the record</h4><p>Watch voice agents think — STT to LLM to TTS, every millisecond mapped.</p></div>
      <div class="rc"><div class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="4" rx="1" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8"/><rect x="4" y="12" width="16" height="4" rx="1" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg></div><h4>Full sessions</h4><p>Replay an entire multi-turn agent journey as one continuous story.</p></div>
      <div class="rc"><div class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="9" cy="9" r="3" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8"/><circle cx="16" cy="15" r="3" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg></div><h4>Your whole team</h4><p>Shared workspaces, roles, and a ledger that knows who did what.</p></div>
      <div class="rc"><div class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 3l7 4v5c0 4-3 7-7 9-4-2-7-5-7-9V7l7-4Z" stroke="#ec4025" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div><h4>Guardrails that learn</h4><p>Catch tomorrow's failure by the shape of yesterday's, across the taxonomy.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="roadline">The recorder becomes a copilot. <a href="https://github.com/tracelane" rel="me noopener">Follow the build on GitHub →</a></div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Pricing (Option B — single-user; no seats/SSO) ===== */}
  <section id="pricing" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap center">
    <div class="eyebrow">Pricing</div>
    <div class="stitle">Priced in traces.</div>
    <p class="lead">Self-host free forever. Hosted starts at $0. Your keys, 0% markup, capped overage.</p>
    <div class="pgrid">
      <div class="pc"><div class="pn">OSS self-host</div><div class="pp">$0<span class="u"> forever</span></div><div class="pq">Apache 2.0 full stack</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 30+ providers · single-node Docker Compose</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Rule-based pre-flight (PR1/PR2/PR4/PR5)</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Tamper-evident audit ledger</li>
      </ul><a href="https://github.com/tracelane" rel="me noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Self-host</a></div>
      <div class="pc"><div class="pn">Free hosted</div><div class="pp">$0</div><div class="pq">10K traces + 10K gateway · 7-day</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 60 RPM · pre-flight policy checks</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Self-verify, free · no commercial use</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Start free</a></div>
      <div class="pc"><div class="pn">Builder</div><div class="pp">$59<span class="u">/mo</span></div><div class="pq">150K traces + 150K gateway · 30-day</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 600 RPM · predictive PR1+PR2+PR4+PR5</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Predictive pre-flight history (read-only)</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Audit ledger + offline verify</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Start Builder</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pgrid" style="margin-top:14px">
      <div class="pc feat"><div class="pn" style="color:var(--lava-deep)">Team</div><div class="pp">$249<span class="u">/mo</span></div><div class="pq">1M traces + 1M gateway · 90-day</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 6K RPM · predictive PR1–PR6</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Tamper-evident promotion record</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Auto-rollback on cost / latency / error · 99% SLA</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-lava" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Start Team</a></div>
      <div class="pc"><div class="pn">Business</div><div class="pp">$899<span class="u">/mo</span></div><div class="pq">5M traces + 5M gateway · 180-day</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 60K RPM · inline ensemble guardrail · 99.9% SLA</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Cohort baselines when n≥30 (roadmap)</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Business</a></div>
      <div class="pc"><div class="pn">Enterprise</div><div class="pp">$2,999<span class="u">+</span></div><div class="pq">25M+ traces · 365-day</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Dedicated tenancy · region pinning · BYOK+CMK</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> 99.95% SLA · 1h response · dedicated CSM</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Contact sales</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pgrid" style="margin-top:14px">
      <div class="pc" style="background:var(--soft);border-color:var(--lava-soft)"><div class="pn" style="color:var(--lava-deep)">Audit SKU · add-on</div><div class="pp">+$999<span class="u">/mo</span></div><div class="pq">Tamper-evident agent ledger for EU AI Act Article 12</div><ul>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> SHA-256 chain + Ed25519 signing · Sigstore Rekor v2 anchoring (best-effort; universal on roadmap)</li>
        <li><span set:html={check}></span> Article-12 export pack · EU data residency</li>
      </ul><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-lava" style="width:100%;justify-content:center">Add the Audit SKU</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pfoot">One gateway call = one trace. Overage $1.20 / 10K, 5× hard cap then 429. OSS self-host free forever.</div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Trust / procurement ===== */}
  <section id="trust" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Security posture</div>
    <div class="stitle">Built for procurement reviews.</div>
    <div class="grid3-cards reveal">
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">release integrity</div><p>Sigstore Cosign keyless signing. SLSA Build L3 provenance. Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived tokens.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">sbom</div><p>CycloneDX SBOM published with every release. Verifiable from GitHub release artifacts.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">vuln scanning</div><p>OSV-Scanner + Grype + Syft on every commit.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">pre-flight policy</div><p>Policy checks run inline at the gateway before the call leaves. V1: schema-violation + tool-definition-drift, fail-open, sub-50ms target.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">transport</div><p>TLS 1.3 minimum. mTLS via SPIFFE/SPIRE for ingest. SSRF defense — RFC1918 + link-local denied.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">standards</div><p>OTel GenAI semconv — tracking the pre-execution judgment / negative-proof proposal (<a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/issues/3244" rel="noopener">#3244</a>).</p></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)">Full security posture: <a href="/security" style="color:var(--lava-deep);text-decoration:underline">/security</a></p>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== FAQ ===== */}
  <section id="faq" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap center">
    <div class="stitle">Frequently asked.</div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>What is Tracelane?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Tracelane is an open-source (Apache 2.0) flight recorder for AI agents: a universal Rust LLM gateway, full-fidelity OpenTelemetry observability, and a tamper-evident audit ledger. Each event is SHA-256 hash-chained and the Merkle root is Ed25519-signed every 100 events, so any trace can be verified offline.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How is Tracelane different from Helicone, LangSmith, or Langfuse?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Tracelane unifies the gateway, observability, pre-flight policy, and a tamper-evident audit ledger in one Rust binary. Helicone, Langfuse, and LangSmith are observability-first — you bring your own gateway and your own guardrails. Tracelane is Apache 2.0 core with a published self-host path; Helicone's gateway is GPL-3.0, Arize Phoenix is ELv2 (no SaaS resale), and LangSmith is closed-source. The audit ledger is hash-chained and Ed25519-signed — no competitor in this category offers cryptographic audit-log integrity at the trace level.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What about LangSmith Engine?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>LangSmith Engine (May 13, 2026) clusters production failures after they happen and drafts pull requests to fix them. Tracelane's pre-flight policy checks flag failure modes at the gateway before the call reaches the provider — sub-50ms target. Engine is locked to the LangSmith trace surface and LangChain-managed inference keys per LangChain's terms of service; Tracelane is neutral OTel ingest with 0% BYOK markup across 30+ providers. Different layer of the agent reliability stack. <a href="/vs/langsmith-engine">Detailed comparison →</a></p></details>
      <details><summary>Is Tracelane really open source?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Yes. The core (Rust gateway, ingest workers, observability backend, pre-flight layer, CLI, SDKs, audit verifiers) is Apache 2.0. The <code>/ee</code> directory contains Tracelane Enterprise License code (paid-tier features behind entitlements). The <code>/spec</code> directory is CC0. Paid features are gated by the workspace_entitlements table at the application layer, not by a license-string compare.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Which providers does Tracelane support?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>At V1: 30+ providers — 6 native adapters (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, AWS Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Cohere) plus any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, including Together, Fireworks, Groq, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, xAI, and Mistral. One canonical wire format across all of them.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does Tracelane support EU AI Act Article 12?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>The Tamper-Evident Agent Ledger add-on ($999/mo) ships at V1. The audit ledger (SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed Merkle root), the EU AI Act Article 12 export pack, and EU data residency are available at V1; the India DPDP Phase II alignment pack and the HIPAA BAA are on the roadmap (BAA on the Business tier; India residency on demand). EU AI Act Annex III obligations were originally scheduled for Aug 2, 2026; the Digital Omnibus political agreement (May 7, 2026) provisionally deferred enforcement to Dec 2, 2027, pending formal adoption (<a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" rel="noopener">details</a>). The ledger ships now so regulated buyers can build audit history before binding enforcement.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What's the latency overhead?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Gateway overhead targets p50 &lt;5ms, p95 &lt;15ms, p99 &lt;25ms (excluding provider time). Pre-flight policy layer targets p99 &lt;50ms on commodity CPU. These are engineering targets — measured numbers publish as the Tracelane Reliability Benchmark v1.0 at launch.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I self-host?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Yes. Docker Compose for development, Helm chart for production. The full ClickHouse + R2 stack runs on a single small Hetzner node. Self-host docs land with V1 — see <a href="/docs">/docs</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>When does V1 launch?<span class="x">+</span></summary><p>Soon — we're finishing the V1 quality gate. Drop your email below and you'll get a single message the day it's live, with the Show HN, X, LinkedIn, and Bluesky links.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Notify ===== */}
  <section id="notify" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="notify reveal">
      <div class="stitle" style="font-size:32px">Get the V1 launch email.</div>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">One email the day we launch. Then nothing unless you opt into product updates. No newsletter, no marketing automation.</p>
      <form id="notify-form" class="nform" method="POST" action="/api/notify">
        <label for="email" class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;left:-999px">email address</label>
        <input id="email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com" />
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-lava">Count me in</button>
      </form>
      <p id="notify-status" class="nstatus" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

